- Current position: “As of [date], Stellar Labs has $2.1M in cash. Our current net cash burn is [confirm], which gives us approximately [confirm] months of runway. Revenue last quarter was $1.8M. While revenue is healthy, our goal is to ensure we have 18–24+ months of runway to reach [next milestone: e.g., EBITDA breakeven / ARR target / product launch / enterprise traction].”
- Primary risks: “The primary risk is an unexpected slowdown in sales closure times and a higher-than-expected fixed cost profile. Key cost drivers: payroll, marketing, vendor contracts, and office commitments.”
- Immediate plan (30 days): “Implement hiring freeze; pause low-ROI growth programs; renegotiate top vendor contracts; run a monthly cash-forecast modeled under three scenarios (base, downside, aggressive savings).”
- Mid-term plan (60–90 days): “Pursue a short bridge (venture debt / convertible) sized to secure 12–18 months while we execute revenue acceleration and operational optimization. If bridge terms are not attractive, pivot to deeper cost optimization to preserve runway while we pursue an equity round.”
- Ask: “Approval to implement the hiring freeze and vendor renegotiation plan immediately, and authorization to pursue a bridge financing package of $X – OR approval to implement deeper cuts if financing options are not viable within 45 days.”

What I can do next for you
- Recalculate scenarios precisely if you confirm the correct current net burn (or upload a 1-page P&L).
- Draft a one-page internal memo or a slide for the board with the numbers, recommended actions, and a clear “ask.”
