Below are actionable runway-extension and cost-reduction options, a recommended prioritization, and a short finance narrative + email templates you can use.

Summary of levers (highest-impact first)
- Revenue acceleration / cash collection
  - Ask/collect prepayments, annual deals/discount for upfront payment — fast way to add immediate cash.
  - Short-term pricing tweaks or temporary upsell packages for existing customers (increase ARPU).
  - Tighten collections & contracts: accelerate invoicing, shorten payment terms, offer small early-pay discounts.
  - Estimated impact: can produce one-time cash injections equal to 1–3 months of revenue if executed aggressively; recurring impact depends on price/upsell scope.

- Bridge financing / debt
  - Consider a small bridge / convertible note or venture debt to cover 6–12 months while you hit milestones.
  - Revenue-based financing can also be viable if gross margins and revenue are steady.
  - Estimated impact: immediate cash injection; cost = interest/dilution.

- Headcount & hiring actions
  - Immediate hiring freeze on non-critical roles.
  - Pause or reduce new contractor spend; convert contractors to part-time if possible.
  - Targeted reductions (if needed) focused on low ROI roles — prioritize preserving revenue-generating teams.
  - Estimated savings: depends on size; often the single largest recurring savings (tens to hundreds of thousands / month).

- Operating expense cuts & vendor renegotiation
  - Audit SaaS stack, cancel unused subscriptions, consolidate licenses.
  - Renegotiate vendor terms, payment schedules, and marketing/media contracts.
  - Reduce discretionary spend (travel, conferences, office perks).
  - Estimated impact: $5K–$50K+/month depending on current spend profile.

- Real estate / office cost optimization
  - Move to hybrid, sublease unused space, renegotiate lease.
  - Estimated impact: variable, can be large if you have significant rent commitments.

- Marketing & GTM efficiency
  - Reallocate marketing budget to highest ROI channels, pause low-performing campaigns.
  - Focus sales on expansion/upsell vs new logo acquisition if CAC is high.
  - Estimated impact: improves cash efficiency; saves marketing spend quickly if paused.

- Product / R&D reprioritization
  - Pause non-critical projects and defer capital spend.
  - Focus on features with near-term revenue or retention impact.
  - Estimated impact: reduces near-term cash outflow and shortens path to revenue-improving releases.

- Strategic options
  - Explore partnership/licensing deals, sell non-core assets or IP, or consider M&A/light options if appropriate.
  - Evaluate strategic investor / corporate partnerships that can bring both capital and distribution.

Prioritization & 90-day plan (practical)
- Days 0–7 (immediate)
  - Confirm/clean the cash model (monthly cash flow, true net burn). I can prepare or revise it if you want.
  - Freeze hiring on all non-essential roles.
  - Pause discretionary spend (marketing campaigns not proven, travel).
