- Objective: “We aim to secure 18–24 months of runway while preserving product momentum and minimizing dilution.”
- Plan (three pillars): “1) Protect cash via immediate operational savings (freeze hiring, cancel non-critical subscriptions, vendor renegotiations). 2) Grow/accelerate cash inflows (convert renewals to annual prepayments, prioritize enterprise deals, tighten AR). 3) If required, secure short-term financing (convertible note / revenue-based financing) to avoid panic cuts and give time to execute.”
- Expected outcome & ask: “If we implement the prioritized actions, we expect to reduce burn by X–Y% within 60 days and extend runway to Z months. Request approval to (a) implement hiring freeze, (b) pause non-essential projects, and (c) explore a bridge financing option up to $[target].”
- Risks & mitigations: short bullets on customer churn risk, product delivery impact, and plan to monitor weekly and report.

