I can help — yes. First, one quick clarification so my recommendations and any scenario work are accurate:

- You wrote Stellar Labs has $2.1M cash, burn $62K/month, and 16 months runway. Those numbers don’t line up: 2.1M / 62K ≈ 34 months runway. If the runway really is 16 months, the implied burn is ~ $131K/month (2.1M / 16). Which set is correct: burn = $62K or runway = 16 months (or is there another cash outflow / committed spend I should know about)? Also confirm whether the $1.8M revenue last quarter is recognized/recurring and what net cash flow from operations looked like last quarter.

While you confirm, here are structured, practical runway-extension and cost-reduction options, plus a ready-to-use finance narrative you can adapt for internal stakeholders.

Quick runways (based on your inputs)
- If burn = $62K/month → runway ≈ 34 months.
- If runway = 16 months (with $2.1M cash) → implied burn ≈ $131K/month.
I’ll use both cases in examples below; tell me which is correct and I’ll build exact scenarios.

Options to extend runway (organized by speed, impact, and pain)

Immediate (30–90 days) — fast impact, low-to-medium pain
- Hiring freeze and pause all non-critical contractors. Savings: depends on headcount plan; typical immediate saving = $10–120K+/month depending on hires paused.
- Cut discretionary spend: travel, events, new marketing experiments. Savings: $5–50K/month.
- Pause or cut low-ROI marketing channels; shift to higher ROI / inbound. Savings: $10–100K+/month depending on spend.
- Renegotiate vendor contracts and software licenses (ask for discounts, credits, extended payment terms). Savings: $5–50K/month.
- Delay non-critical capital projects and R&D initiatives. Savings vary.

Medium term (3–9 months) — structural, moderate impact
- Consolidate SaaS tools and eliminate redundancies. Savings: $5–30K/month.
- Move to more flexible workforce (shift fixed contractors to part-time / milestone-based). Savings: $10–80K/month.
- Office footprint optimization (hybrid/remote-first, sublease excess space). Savings: $10–50K/month.
- Implement tighter procurement approvals and monthly budget reviews.
- Introduce performance-linked hiring and milestone-based vendor payments.

High impact but higher pain (3–6 months)
- Workforce restructuring (layoffs or furloughs) — fast biggest savings but high morale/legal cost. Example: removing 5 FTEs at avg fully-loaded ~$15K/month saves ~$75K/month.
- Salary freezes or temporary pay reductions (short-term). Savings depend on scale.

Revenue & cash-acceleration moves (can materially extend runway)
- Offer discounts for annual prepayments, customer financing, or early renewals. Immediate cash inflow; short-term revenue impact.
- Push enterprise deals and upsells—prioritize short-cycle higher-ARPA accounts.
- Short-term pricing adjustments for new customers (carefully tested).
- Implement or accelerate collections: tighten net terms, invoice faster, offer small discounts for early payment.
- Explore revenue-based financing or factoring for receivables.

