- Vendor payment terms and price renegotiation — ask for discounts or extended payment schedules. (2–10% savings, plus cash flow relief.)
- Cloud & infra optimization (right‑sizing, reserved instances, autoscaling). (10–30% on cloud spend if material.)

Near term (30–90 days; medium impact)
- Convert monthly customers to annual prepayment offers (discounts for upfront cash). (Improves near-term cash.)
- Reduce contractor / consultant spend; shift to outcome-based contracts.
- Supplier financing, invoice factoring, accelerate receivables (if you have receivables).
- Temporary salary deferrals or reduced hours programs with clear timeline (sensitive, but can be effective).

Bigger / strategic (longer-term or higher cost/dilution)
- Raise a bridge round or a small extension (equity) — dilutive but buys time.
- Venture debt (if you have predictable revenue and assets for covenants) — less dilutive, interest + covenants.
- Strategic partnerships, channel agreements, or commercial deals that include upfront payments.
- Asset sales or monetizing non-core IP.

